    docs: document submit 503 solver_unavailable; drop stale queue-until-restart claim. Addresses OB-GAP-069
    
    docs/api-reference.md: add `503` (`solver_unavailable`) to the POST /api/v1/problems/submit
    status set and document the response body plus the no-queue-entry behavior. The handler
    rejects before any queue write (internal/api/handlers.go:206-210) and the check runs ahead of
    body parsing, so the status applies to JSON and multipart submissions alike.
    
    docs/integration.md: replace the false "submissions will stay in the queue until the server is
    restarted" guidance (the handler never queues while solver_available is false) with the real
    behavior — HTTP 503, error code solver_unavailable, no submission id, nothing in
    GET /api/v1/queue — and keep the operator restart guidance. Adds the 503 case to the submit
    status summary.
    
    Documented submit status set now 200 / 400 / 409 / 500 / 503, matching the writeError statuses
    in handleSubmitProblem (400 invalid_request, 500 internal_error, 503 solver_unavailable) plus
    the 409 duplicate path (ingest.StatusForHTTP). Docs-only change; no Go code touched.
    
